      "side": 1,
      "message": "```suggestion\nDevice attestation is a way for an app to ask if a phone and it\u0027s software is legitimate. Your phone answers with the creation of proofs, like a signed report on it\u0027s own state with details like what operating system (OS) it runs and whether it\u0027s been modified. The app, or the server behind it, then decides whether or not to trust your device based on those proofs.\n```",
