      "writtenOn": "2026-11-09T20:07:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```suggestion\nThe main name when we talk about attestation in Android is [Play Integrity](https://developer.android.com/google/play/integrity) which is Google’s solution,  and only approves operating systems by OEMs (device manufactorers) who include Google\u0027s app suite, including Google Play Services.\n\nAside from the accessibility of Play Integrity to non-Google systems, Play Integrity is not necessarily bad. However, the problem is how its used by some applications: many apps treat not certified by Google as unsafe, and lock out secure, privacy respecting OSes like CalyxOS while doing little to stop dedicated attackers.\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 278
      },
      "revId": "d38f5c7099b109be1981d6d9df3991953beeed20",
      "serverId": "35266860-6252-469c-a67d-185064479fc0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a088ba01_85cda03f",
        "filename": "pages/docs/guide/app-compatibility/index.md",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 15,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000136
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-09T20:07:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```suggestion\nPlay Integrity is the biggest obstacle to app compatibility with CalyxOS and other Android-based operating systems. Apps would work fine without it, however we are locked out by every app/server that decides to opt-in to using Play Integrity.\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 15,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 15,
        "endChar": 50
