      "lineNbr": 17,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000136
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-09T20:07:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```suggestion\nPlay Integrity has three attestation levels:\n- BASIC: The device passes basic checks for tampering. This level is the easiest to spoof and CalyxOS reaches BASIC.\n- DEVICE: This level requires Google approving the OS (i.e. certification). On newer Android versions, this also requires a locked bootloader with booting setup that Google recognizes. CalyxOS isn\u0027t certified by Google so it doesn\u0027t pass, even though it runs with a locked bootloader.\n- STRONG. Requires [hardware attestation](https://developer.android.com/privacy-and-security/security-key-attestation) which uses secure hardware on your device to create a proof of the OS running on your device, and cannot be easily spoofed.\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 17,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 17,
        "endChar": 415
      },
      "revId": "d38f5c7099b109be1981d6d9df3991953beeed20",
