        "id": 1000136
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-11-09T20:07:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "```suggestion\nAn app may not always be clear as to what is failing: they may just log you out, give a vague error, crash when opened or behave oddly. When that is the case, the best thing to do go through the list above and check each item. Of course, some apps will always require DEVICE and STRONG integrity, and as such will not work on CalyxOS.\n\n#### Not all banks enforce it\nMany of our users have no issues using banking apps, as their banks do not enforce aggressive attestation like Play Integrity.\n\n## How do I know if an app I need/want to use will work?\nA very useful resource is [Plexus](https://plexus.techlore.tech/): a crowdsourced compatibility database for devices running microG, which spans across many alternative operating systems. Users share any needed steps to get apps working, and their experience with the app. It has an F-Droid app where you can see the reviews for the apps or help contribute to it when you\u0027re using CalyxOS!\n```",
